@drisspg , can I work on this?
Looks like an Inductor codegen bug. Constexprs land in triton_meta["constants"] and get emitted via triton_meta={triton_meta!r}, so NamedTuple repr embeds the user class name and the generated module never defines it. Plain tuples work. I'll dig into it more.

Also Should dataclass / other types with non self contained reprs be in scope too, or NamedTuple only?

@aditew01 There is only one data point at the moment, but I think the number looks good where you can see the aggregated execution time has dropped back to June 22nd level before the regression.

<img width="1167" height="287" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a10e1b41-53d2-4c4d-a2aa-96209800bda1" />

Let me know if you can independently confirm this too, we can wait for a couple more day to have more data points
